[m
    docs(task-04): initialise repository with README, templates and branch policy[m
    [m
    Make the repository usable by someone who has never seen it, and make the[m
    workflow rules explicit before feature work starts in Task 5.[m
    [m
    README[m
    - Rewritten as a full entry point: why the project exists, what it does mapped to[m
      the user stories, technology table with rationale, quick start, the complete[m
      externalised-configuration table, project structure and documentation index.[m
    [m
    .gitignore[m
    - Expanded to 43 grouped rules. Three deliberate decisions: `!docs/evidence/**/*.log`[m
      negates the blanket `*.log` so evidence logs stay tracked alongside the[m
      screenshots rendered from them; `data/` and `*.mv.db` keep the disposable H2[m
      database out so repository state does not depend on who ran the app last; and[m
      secrets (.env, *.key, vault passwords, credentials.properties) are excluded[m
      because registry and deployment credentials come from Jenkins credentials[m
      binding, never from the repository.[m
    [m
    GitHub metadata[m
    - Three issue templates with blank issues disabled, so every issue arrives[m
      actionable: user story (backlog ID, Given/When/Then, epic, MoSCoW, points and[m
      the data-testid hooks Selenium will need), bug report (expected vs actual, the[m
      violated acceptance criterion, and a commitment to a failing test before the[m
      fix), and DevOps task (lifecycle stage, tool, and which evidence artefact must[m
      be produced).[m
    - Pull request template requiring verification commands actually run and their[m
      real result, followed by the Definition of Done as a checklist.[m
    [m
    CONTRIBUTING.md[m
    - Branch policy: main and develop as long-lived; short-lived branches named[m
      <type>/<backlog-id>-<description> with the backlog ID mandatory for feature,[m
      bugfix and hotfix; integrate develop into your branch, never the reverse.[m
    - Conventional Commits with the accepted type list and examples of what is not[m
      acceptable; annotated semantic version tags.[m
